From ccbd5d727b76540399474c12c13c3fdfd627fee5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 17:26:14 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] metrics: MDBX database size and commit latency

All of the node's databases (chainstate, block index, txindex,
blockfilterindex, coinstatsindex) are MDBX environments behind
CDBWrapper. How large they grow and how long their commits take - the
cost of every UTXO flush and of each index write - was not visible.

- fullnode_db_size_bytes{db}: the environment's current geometry
  (mdbx_env_info_ex mi_geo.current, the data file's size), read after
  each commit.
- fullnode_db_commit_seconds{db}: from the write transaction's start to
  its commit (and the sync, when the batch asked for one), in
  CDBWrapper::WriteBatch, the only runtime write path. _count counts
  commits.

db is one of chainstate, block_index, txindex, blockfilterindex,
coinstatsindex, other, classified once from the database's path when it
opens (MetricDatabaseIndex). Two databases of one kind (a snapshot
chainstate beside the background one) share a size series; the last
commit sets it.

Cardinality: 6 size series, 6 histogram label sets (20 buckets, 50 us to
120 s).

Hot paths: none per transaction. Each commit (one per index block, one
per UTXO flush) adds two clock reads, a ring push and an mdbx_env_info_ex
call with -metrics, and one acquire load without; no lock is added.

Evidence:
- metrics_tests/database_labels (each database's path), dbwrapper_tests
  pass.
- interface_metrics_storage.py: with the three indexes on, all six
  database label values are present; after five blocks and
  gettxoutsetinfo (a flush), chainstate, block_index, txindex and
  coinstatsindex commit counts grew and their sizes are positive;
  blockfilterindex committed; "other" did not.

Not tested: sizes after compaction or growth steps; commit latency
values themselves (only that they are recorded); the snapshot chainstate.
